feat(twin): inherit archetypes from the twin hub

openrappter can now adopt a twin archetype from kody-w/rapp-twin-hub — a
reusable description of HOW a twin behaves (voice, working habits, mandate)
that never contains anyone's personal details.

    openrappter twin inherit founder

Inheritance flows hub -> device only. There is no function in archetype.ts
that sends a profile anywhere, and a test asserts that rather than a comment
promising it.

- resolveArchetype walks `extends` to the root and merges back down
- boundaries are ADDITIVE: a child may add a restriction but never remove one,
  and a mayDo that contradicts an ancestor's mustAsk/neverDo is dropped.
  Without that rule anyone could publish a friendly-looking archetype that
  quietly disarms everything downstream of it.
- validateArchetype rejects unknown fields outright, so a crafted archetype
  cannot smuggle a field an older client would store blindly
- cycles, missing parents and chains deeper than 8 are errors, not warnings
- inherit() is additive and idempotent: identity, roles, context and accounts
  are never touched, the owner's own words come first in every merged list,
  and `inherits` records the lineage so a boundary's origin is always visible
- httpLoader is read-only (no method, no body) and rejects an id that could
  escape the archetype path

Kept deliberately in step with the Python implementation in the hub; both are
run over the same archetypes and must agree.

Fixed a real bug found end to end: `inherit` used vaultFor(command.parent!),
which is right for nested subcommands like `set voice` but wrong for a direct
child of `twin`. The shared --home resolved to the wrong vault, so the command
printed "Inherited base -> founder" while the profile on disk was untouched.
Reporting success for work that did not happen is the worst failure available,
so there are now two guards: a save/load round trip, and a check that no direct
child of `twin` uses the two-level form. Verified by reintroducing the bug and
watching both fail.

64 twin tests. Full suite: same 3 pre-existing gateway failures, no regressions.

